    {
      "challengedBy": [],
      "claim": "The helper returns `refreshTokenResponse` (the full `safeParse` result), yet callers in `googlecalendar`, `office365calendar`, `salesforce`, and `zoomvideo` assign it to `key`/`parsedToken` and then read `.success` or `.data` inconsistently. In `GoogleCalendarService`, `key` is written directly into Prisma as if it were the parsed credential payload, which breaks the caller/callee contract and can persist the wrong shape.",
      "confidence": 0.7200000286102295,
      "discoveredBy": [
        "final-synthesis"
